> I hear people complain that Gehennom is boring.  But really, how long
> are you actually in Gehennom?

I usually play speed monks, so by that time I've polymorphed up
spellbooks of magic mapping and detect treasure, and obtained intrinsic
teleport and teleport control (level 17 for monks). And of course the
first wish goes for the Eye of the Aethiopica, which lets you teleport
much more frequently. After doing the Valley, I usually level teleport
to find Vlad, then teleport again to the bottom, find the VS, then up
to Rodney. Oftentimes, I only encounter many of the dungeon levels on
the way up and cross them in five or so turns:

drop the amulet
cast magic mapping
pick up the amulet
^T to the upstairs
go up

Done this way, you can do Gehennom in less than an hour, if you aren't
counting the Valley of the Dead.



